s when I weaken it. For the other three I weakened each one and the capture tests stayed green:\n- **Checkpoint accepted as provider quiescence.** I let `ax_checkpoint_boundary` count as provider proof, and `TestCaptureRejectsCheckpointBoundaryAsProviderProof` still passed. That test passes no Runner, so it is refused earlier with \"Git assembly runner is required\", which has the same error code. It never reaches the check it's named after.\n- **The hold isn't re-checked at the end.** I disabled the closing `QuiesceBarrierProven` check, and separately removed the check that the input-closure receipt is from the current incarnation. Both changes survived every capture test.\n- **A stopped capture no longer has to stay stopped.** Allowing the closing state to be `quiescing` also survived. This is less serious, because no owner transition goes from stopped to quiescing.\n\nMeasured: 1 of 4 coordinator checks is pinned by a narrowed mutant that its named test kills when run alone.\n\n**What held up:**\n- **Source change during capture.** Both of my weakened versions of the change check in `gitsnap` assembly failed `TestAssemblySourceChangesAndRetry` when run alone. The harmless control changes survived, so the harness can report a survivor.\n- **Refresh.** Both replayed checkpoints have good signatures. `task-board.config.json` is byte-identical to the base. Every path only trunk changed is identical to the new base.\n- **Registry.** Every trunk row is present except the §10.4 gap row, which this Story replaces on purpose. `tracecheck` reports 106/597, the same as the README, and changing that figure in a README copy makes the pin test fail.\n- **Lint.** `go vet`, Windows `go vet` and `gofmt` are clean.\n- **Tests.** The gitsnap, canonicaljson, traceability and provhost packages pass. specpin passes when run in the live worktree.\n\n**Not verified this round:**\n- The whole `tmuxserver` package hit Go's default 10-minute test timeout, so it didn't finish. Only its capture tests were run separately, and they pass.\n- I did not rerun the importer outcome comparison, the `-count=3` determinism check, or a separate digest re-derivation.\n- I didn't test manifest closure, path safety or byte identity directly.\n\n**Notes that don't block:**\n- `TestCaptureStopPointStateDomain` has no row where capture is allowed, and every row fails with the same code, so allowing `parked` doesn't fail it. Another named test does catch that change.\n- The Story changed the landed `probe.go` Dial so a missing socket counts as stale only when its directory exists. No spec citation is given for that.\n- `sameObservation` ignores marshal errors, so two failed marshals compare as equal.\n\n**Rework for the producer:**\n- Make each coordinator test reach its own check: supply a Runner, Assembly and a valid boundary body, and assert the refusal detail, not just the code.\n- Ship one weakened mutant per check, each killed by its named test run alone.\n- Add allowed rows for `quiescing` with a boundary and for `stopped` to the state test.\n- Cite the spec for the `probe.go` change, or move it to its own task.\n\nFiles attached to the task:\n- `TASK-260830-2xt6fd_review-verdict-rev1.md`\n- `TASK-260830-2xt6fd_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`","ttft_ms":2232,"type":"result","duration_ms":1518489,"uuid":"934b5357-bd06-43d0-bac2-006e119da222","ttft_stream_ms":1571,"time_to_request_ms":42,"first_content_frame_ms":1571,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
